---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/content';
import { siteConfig, topics } from '../data/site';
---

<MainLayout
  title="About"
  description="The questions, subjects and working philosophy behind NegotiatedTruth, a personal journal by Cătălin Criveteanu."
>
  <section class="shell page-intro">
    <span class="eyebrow">Behind the journal</span>
    <h1>I'm Cătălin.</h1>
    <p>
      NegotiatedTruth is my personal journal about strategy, technology and AI:
      how ideas become decisions, and what happens when those decisions meet the
      work.
    </p>
  </section>
  <div class="prose legal about-copy">
    <p>
      I’m interested in the gap between an appealing idea and something that
      works. A good argument can make a choice feel obvious. The constraints,
      the people involved and the consequences often make it more interesting.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is a place to work through that complexity in public: to connect
      ideas, examine assumptions and leave a record of what holds up when we try
      it.
    </p>
    <h2>Why “NegotiatedTruth”?</h2>
    <p>
      A decision often sits between several reasonable perspectives. The
      technical answer, the business priority and the human experience may each
      reveal a different part of the problem.
    </p>
    <p>
      The name is an invitation to bring those perspectives together. I want to
      make the trade-offs visible, explain the reasoning and leave room to
      revise a view when the evidence changes.
    </p>
    <h2>The questions I’m exploring</h2>
    <div class="about-subjects">
      {topics.map((topic) => (
        <section>
          <h3>
            <a href={href(`topics/${topic.id}/`)}>{topic.name} ↗</a>
          </h3>
          <p class="subject-question">{topic.question}</p>
          <p>{topic.editorialFocus}</p>
        </section>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2>How I approach the writing</h2>
    <p>
      A point of view should be clear enough to challenge. The aim is to show
      the reasoning behind a conclusion, distinguish evidence from
      interpretation and be explicit about what remains uncertain.
    </p>
    <p>
      Some pieces will follow an argument at length. Others will capture a small
      observation or test an idea with a diagram and a worked example. The
      format should help the question, and the question should lead somewhere
      useful.
    </p>
    <h2>What you’ll find here</h2>
    <ul class="format-descriptions">
      <li>
        <strong>Essays</strong> — an argument developed carefully, with room for
        its limits and implications.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Field notes</strong> — a focused observation, a practical
        question or something worth returning to.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Visual stories and experiments</strong> — a way to make a
        system, relationship or trade-off easier to inspect.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href={href('writing/')}>Explore the writing ↗</a>
    </p>
    <aside class="about-preview">
      <h2>A journal in the making</h2>
      <p>
        The articles in this preview are clearly labelled sample writing. The
        original articles and a fuller personal biography will replace the
        provisional material before launch.
      </p>
    </aside>
    <p class="about-elsewhere">
      <a href={siteConfig.github}>Find me on GitHub ↗</a>
      <br />
      <a href={href('rss.xml')}>Follow new writing via RSS ↗</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
